  "challenge": "A hard REJECT over-reads FR-003. All three line items match the item master exactly (WidgetA $250, GadgetX $750, WidgetB $500), WidgetA/WidgetB quantities sit within standing stock, and tax is a clean 5% of the stated subtotal—consistent with a real catalog quote, not fabricated noise. get_vendor_record and get_vendor_invoice_history only show a never-before-seen supplier, which under VN-001 is an onboarding/verification trigger, not automatic fraud; PO-001 is an approval-threshold flag and IN-003 an inventory constraint. FR-003 is only MEDIUM, and a famous-address placeholder on an otherwise coherent first-time invoice has an innocent reading (template/default address) that a human vendor check could clear—so the packet supports escalation for master setup and manager approval more than a disqualifying fraud reject.",
  "proposed_outcome": "ESCALATE",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["FR-003", "VN-001", "PO-001", "IN-003"]
}
